From: Long Way Home <noreply@long-way-home.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] measure the content limits a level spends

Task A of the engine-content-headroom brief (docs/gates.md, the RPG-X headroom item): the
configstring budget was raised to 4096 in patch 0004 without measuring what retail or the stitched
ship actually spend. This adds the missing instrument, which is logging only and silent unless
`developer` is set -- so with it unset (the default) the bridge behaves and saves exactly as before.

At every SP spawn it prints the loaded level's own content registration, read from the bridge's
own configstring table after the game has spawned its entities:

  EFSP: SP_SpawnServer: content: 104 configstrings of 4096 (bridge table CS_MAX 1024):
        46 models of 256, 53 sounds of 256; gentities 564 of 4096

The bridge table is sized by the literal CS_MAX (1024), while MAX_CONFIGSTRINGS (what the gamestate
and the save format are sized against) is 4096; both are stated because SP content capacity is
bounded by the table and by MAX_MODELS + MAX_SOUNDS, not by MAX_CONFIGSTRINGS alone.
---
diff --git a/EFAndroid-SP/app/jni/sp/sp_bridge.cpp b/EFAndroid-SP/app/jni/sp/sp_bridge.cpp
--- a/EFAndroid-SP/app/jni/sp/sp_bridge.cpp
+++ b/EFAndroid-SP/app/jni/sp/sp_bridge.cpp
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 
 #include "q_shared.h"
 #include "g_public.h"
+#include "bg_public.h"           // CS_MODELS / CS_SOUNDS / CS_PLAYERS (the content configstring blocks)
 #include "tr_types.h"             // glconfig_t, refEntity_t, refdef_t
 #include "../cgame/cg_public.h"   // cgameImport_t (CG_*), snapshot_t
 #include "../client/vmachine.h"   // cgameExport_t (CG_INIT, CG_DRAW_ACTIVE_FRAME)
@@ -658,6 +659,24 @@
     ge->Init( mapname, "", checksum, entstring, g_levelTime, Sys_Milliseconds(), Sys_Milliseconds(),
               (SavedGameJustLoaded_e)0, qfalse );
     blog("SP_SpawnServer: ge->Init done. num_entities=%d linked=%d\n", ge->num_entities, g_numLinked);
+    // Content-limit instrument (docs/prior-art-rpg-x.md, the headroom item): how much of the
+    // configstring budget THIS level spends, so authored content is measured against the ceiling
+    // instead of assumed. The bridge's own table is sized CS_MAX (models + sounds + players), but
+    // MAX_CONFIGSTRINGS is what the gamestate and the save format are sized against, so both are
+    // stated. Logging only, and only with `developer` set, so retail behaviour and saves are
+    // untouched with it unset (the default).
+    if ( Cvar_VariableIntegerValue( "developer" ) ) {
+        int csTotal = 0, csModels = 0, csSounds = 0, ci;
+        for ( ci = 0; ci < CS_MAX; ci++ ) {
+            if ( !g_configstrings[ci][0] ) continue;
+            csTotal++;
+            if ( ci >= CS_MODELS && ci < CS_SOUNDS ) csModels++;
+            else if ( ci >= CS_SOUNDS && ci < CS_PLAYERS ) csSounds++;
+        }
+        blog("SP_SpawnServer: content: %d configstrings of %d (bridge table CS_MAX %d): %d models of %d, %d sounds of %d; gentities %d of %d\n",
+             csTotal, MAX_CONFIGSTRINGS, CS_MAX, csModels, MAX_MODELS, csSounds, MAX_SOUNDS,
+             ge->num_entities, MAX_GENTITIES);
+    }
     // C1 (reclaim path only): bring the renderer we tore down above back up BEFORE SP_StartClient's CG_INIT
     // loads the new world. Mirrors SP_FinishTransition's SP_FillGlConfig()+SPR_InitRenderer() ordering. On the
     // first spawn the boot renderer is already up, so skip (CG_INIT loads the world as before).
